action,x,y,origin,button,key,micros,note,platform
# P92 on AppKit: what a click in the text field does, then text selected by dragging and copied.
# The field starts as "hello" and, as the window opens, has the focus with its text selected.
# CLICK: a click right of the text, then X typed. A click that selects everything leaves "X"; one
# that places the caret leaves "helloX". Command-Z puts "hello" back.
# DRAG: pressed at the start of "hello" (frame x 82) and moved right 5 points at a time to x 116 past
# its end, then let go -- a selection made by relative moves, as a person drags. Command-C copies it,
# the right arrow moves the caret to the end, Command-V pastes: "hellohello".
# Expected "field" lines in p92-commands.log, in order: helloX | hello | hellohello.
# P92 在 AppKit 上：點擊文字欄位的行為，以及用拖曳選取文字再複製。欄位起始為 hello,視窗開啟時已取得焦點並全選。
# CLICK:點在文字右側再打 X;點擊若全選會剩 X,若只放游標會是 helloX。DRAG:在 hello 開頭按下，每次往右 5 點拖過結尾後放開，
# ⌘C 複製、→ 移到結尾、⌘V 貼上，得到 hellohello。p92-commands.log 的 field 各行應依序為 helloX、hello、hellohello。
